{
  "manufacturer": "Novelan",
  "manufacturer_slug": "novelan",
  "model": "Novelan heat pump controller via Novelan GLT (Modbus TCP)",
  "model_slug": "novelan-glt-modbus-tcp",
  "short_model": "Novelan GLT Modbus",
  "aliases": [
    "Novelan GLT",
    "83055703",
    "ait-deutschland GLT"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Heat pump",
  "applies_to": "Novelan (ait-deutschland) heat pumps whose heating and heat pump controller runs software V1.74 / V2.74 / V3.76 / V4.76 or later, with the GLT function licensed via the Novelan GLT USB dongle; operating manual 83055703hDE.",
  "summary": "With the GLT licence active, the Novelan heating and heat pump controller is a Modbus TCP slave on port 502 at the controller's own IP address. Discrete inputs show utility block, smart-grid and compressor/heater states; input registers give temperatures, pressures, running hours, plant status, faults, output and 32-bit heat and energy counters; coils reset faults and force pumps on; holding registers take outdoor temperature, setpoints, operating modes, smart-grid state and heating-curve settings.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual warns that registers are 0-based: the printed ID is the wire address (input register 0 = mean outdoor temperature, holding register 0 = outdoor temperature)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Controller software V1.74/V2.74/V3.76/V4.76 or later for Modbus TCP",
  "source": {
    "title": "Zubehör für Wärmepumpen - Anbindung an eine Gebäudeleittechnik via BACnet/IP | ModBus/TCP - Novelan GLT (Betriebsanleitung)",
    "doc_number": "83055703hDE",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://forum.iobroker.net/assets/uploads/files/1732701258966-83055703hde_novelan_glt.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "p. 3 software requirements; p. 4 licence; p. 17 Modbus specification (0-based note, port 502); pp. 18-22 data points (discrete inputs, input registers, coils, holding registers); p. 23 abbreviations"
  },
  "notes": [
    "ait-deutschland / Novelan do not appear to host this manual publicly; the link is an unaltered copy of the manufacturer's PDF posted on the ioBroker forum.",
    "The manual calls all registers integer values without stating signedness. Temperatures and the holding offset 23 are listed as INT16 because the holding outdoor temperature accepts -200 (= -20.0 °C) and the offset -50; the input-register temperatures have no printed range, so negative readings assume two's complement.",
    "'Auflösung 10' means tenths (scale 0.1) and 'Auflösung 100' hundredths (scale 0.01). Heat and energy counters are printed in 'kW/h' and are taken as kWh.",
    "Each 32-bit counter is split into High and Low registers; the manual says to shift High 16 bits left and add Low, with High at the lower ID, so they are listed as UINT32 high word first.",
    "Data points marked * in the manual exist only on units with LIN and/or Modbus components; greyed points need a comfort/extension or ventilation board. Values for points not visible on the controller display are invalid.",
    "Discrete inputs exist only for IDs 0-7. Coil 1 is reserved and left out.",
    "Coils read 0 = off and 1 = on. Writing 1 forces the output on; writing 0 hands it back to automatic control."
  ],
